From 1ac0ebbc00eea0f981a52167fe55ba9f2bb2284f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Corey <coreysho@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 02:55:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Read a whole packet: the inbound buffer matches the server's

Client.in was Packet.alloc(1) = 5000 bytes, and a variable-length server
packet is read whole into it - "this.stream.read(this.in.data, 0, this.psize)"
- so the biggest packet the server can send has to fit or the read walks off
the end of the array. An inv update costs up to 7 bytes a slot, which capped a
transmitted inv at 713 slots; the bank is now 1410. alloc(2) is 30000.

The server's outgoing buffer was raised to match in Engine-TS. Either end left
at 5000 is a crash on a full bank, so the two go together.

Nothing else changes. The client already zeroed every inv slot past the size
it was given, which is what lets the engine transmit only the occupied part of
a 1410-slot bank rather than all of it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WTo3qFuhgbaA3yymZcTW7m
---
 src/main/java/jagex2/client/Client.java | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/main/java/jagex2/client/Client.java b/src/main/java/jagex2/client/Client.java
index 8e829e5..e7187eb 100644
--- a/src/main/java/jagex2/client/Client.java
+++ b/src/main/java/jagex2/client/Client.java
@@ -602,7 +602,12 @@ public class Client extends GameShell {
 	public String[] menuOption = new String[500];
 
 	@ObfuscatedName("client.yh")
-	public Packet in = Packet.alloc(1);
+	// alloc(2) is 30000 bytes, not alloc(1)'s 5000. A variable-length server packet is read whole
+	// into this buffer - "this.stream.read(this.in.data, 0, this.psize)" - so the largest packet
+	// the server can send has to fit in it or the read walks off the end of the array. An inv
+	// update costs up to 7 bytes a slot, so 5000 bytes capped a transmitted inv at 713 slots;
+	// the bank is 1410. The server's outgoing buffer (ClientSocket.out) was raised to match.
+	public Packet in = Packet.alloc(2);
 
 	@ObfuscatedName("client.zh")
 	public int[][] bfsCost = new int[104][104];
